## Pulsation of R Draconis {#rdra}

R Draconis is a Mira variable with a catalogued period of [[e28s.rdra_period_d|f0]] days. It saturates the detector, so it is measured in an annulus around the saturated core, with errors set by comparison stars. A sine fit to the pictures measured first predicted a maximum at 4.4–5.0 µm on [[e28s.rdra_predicted_max_mjd|date]]. In [[e28s.rdra_n_pictures_confirmation]] pictures not used for that fit ([[deriveds.rdra_n_pictures_D6]] of them at 4.4–5.0 µm), the star varies by [[e28s.rdra_D6_semi_amplitude_mag|f2]] ± [[e28s.rdra_D6_semi_amplitude_mag_err|f2]] mag either side of its mean, with a fitted maximum on [[e28s.rdra_D6_t_max_mjd|date]] ± [[e28s.rdra_D6_t_max_err_d|f0]] days, [[e28s.rdra_D6_offset_from_prediction_d|f1]] days after the prediction. The light curve departs from a sine: with errors scaled to the scatter about the fit, the amplitude is [[e28s.rdra_posthoc_D6_z_errors_scaled_by_fit|f0]]σ. At 3.8–4.4 µm the new pictures cover too few dates for a fit.

[Methods, section 7](methods.html#variability)

![Light curve of R Draconis](figs/v2/e28_rdra.svg "Brightness relative to the mean at 4.4–5.0 µm (a) and 3.8–4.4 µm (b), in 30-day bins: pictures not used for the prediction (filled circles) and pictures used for it (open circles), with the predicted curve (dash-dot), the fitted sine (solid; a only) and the scatter of comparison stars (grey band). Bars are 1σ.")

## Hydrogen emission lines {#e20}

SPHEREx covers the Paschen-α (1.875 µm) and Brackett-α (4.05 µm) hydrogen lines. Of [[e20.M_total]] stars that Gaia classifies as Herbig Ae/Be or Be stars, [[e20.N_total]] show an excess in these lines, against [[e20.control_fp]] of [[e20.control_testable]] ordinary stars of similar brightness in the same pictures. At SPHEREx's spectral resolution, emission from the star cannot be separated from emission by surrounding gas.

